    "kicker": "GPU performance",
    "image": "images/lead_2026-11-02.jpg",
    "title": "Open-source UEFI tool unlocks Nvidia's half-speed tensor limiter on RTX 20/30/40 cards",
    "summary": "The nv-uefi-unlocker project boots from a USB drive before the Nvidia driver loads and removes the half-speed Tensor Core throttle on RTX 20, 30 and 40 series desktop and laptop GPUs, lifting FP16 matrix math performance by up to 65% on Windows and Linux. Blackwell RTX 50 series is not covered. It is free throughput for the huge installed base of last-gen cards powering local LLM rigs.",
    "source": "Tom's Hardware",
    "date": "2026-11-01",
    "url": "https://tomshardware.com/pc-components/gpus/open-source-usb-tool-unlocks-nvidias-half-speed-gpu-ai-limiter-on-windows-lifts-gpus-fp16-math-performance-up-to-65-percent-uefi-unlocker-covers-rtx-20-30-and-40-series-desktops-and-laptops",
    "scout_source": "hardware"
  },
